{"id":"kolu-ci-root","ord":"a0","title":"kolu-ci — the Incus pool venue","desc":"The CI venue's own page: the pool of Incus containers (kolu-ci-*) odu runs dispatch to over ssh (reached via a 127.0.0.1 proxy device, user toor). Downtimes and venue incidents are filed under `downtimes`, evidence-first, for the Incus admin.","created":"2026-08-29T14:22:59-04:00"}
{"id":"kolu-ci-downtimes","parent":"kolu-ci-root","ord":"a0","title":"downtimes","desc":"One child per incident: what died, when (UTC and ET), what was running, the exact client-side symptom, and what the host itself says. For the Incus admin.","created":"2026-08-29T14:22:59-04:00"}
{"id":"downtime-2026-08-29a","parent":"kolu-ci-downtimes","ord":"a0","title":"2026-08-29 ~15:28–15:31 UTC — kolu-ci-9: ssh transport died mid-e2e; the whole odu run lost","desc":"**When:** ~15:28–15:31 UTC (11:28–11:31 ET), 2026-08-29.\n**Host:** kolu-ci-9. **Running:** olai PR #427's CI (head 01da4e9d), e2e leg ~2m19s in.\n**Client-side symptom:** the odu coordinator's ssh lane to kolu-ci-9 dropped (keep-alive lost); every log subscription errored at once. The (then-unfixed) odu coordinator crashed on teardown — run history lost, only per-node logs surviving. Exact crash transcript preserved in the orchestrator vault, briefs/odu-teardown-crash.md (the investigation): `⚠ errored e2e@x86_64-linux 2m19s` then eight `logTail: append … after its log ended` throws and Bun's crash footer.\n**Consequence contained:** the coordinator crash was root-caused and fixed same day — juspay/odu#93 (merged 17:31Z): a dying transport now errors ONE node. The HOST-side drop itself is what remains unexplained.","created":"2026-08-29T14:22:59-04:00","custom":{"host":"kolu-ci-9"}}
{"id":"downtime-2026-08-29b","parent":"kolu-ci-downtimes","ord":"a1","title":"2026-08-29 ~17:34–17:38 UTC — kolu-ci-9 again: same ssh death, second run lost its e2e leg","desc":"**When:** ~17:34–17:38 UTC (13:34–13:38 ET), 2026-08-29 — about two hours after the first.\n**Host:** kolu-ci-9 (SAME container). **Running:** olai PR #428's CI (head 0d90ff81, seq 1), e2e leg mid-flight.\n**Client-side symptom:** identical shape — the lane transport died mid-e2e; the CI watcher classified it \"a dead lane host — not master drift, not a code fix to make.\" Every node that had finished was green; only the in-flight e2e errored. A fresh run (seq 2) on the pool went 10/10 — the failure does not follow the code.\n**Pattern:** both incidents on kolu-ci-9, both during the e2e leg (the longest, most network-chatty node), roughly 2h apart.","created":"2026-08-29T14:22:59-04:00","custom":{"host":"kolu-ci-9"}}
{"id":"downtime-2026-08-29-hostprobe","parent":"kolu-ci-downtimes","ord":"a2","title":"The host's own testimony (probed 18:21 UTC): never rebooted, healthy — the container did not die; the ssh path did","desc":"Probe from the orchestrator over the same ssh path, 18:21 UTC:\n\n```\nkolu-ci-9\n 18:21:59  up 6 days 22:09,  0 users,  load average: 0.78, 0.55, 0.67\nreboot   system boot  6.12.85   Sat Aug 22 20:12   still running\nMem: 125Gi total, 103Gi free\n```\n\n**Reading:** the container has been up since Aug 22 — through BOTH incidents — with no reboot, no OOM pressure now, near-idle load. So the failures were not container crashes: the break is in the ssh path (the Incus proxy device forwarding 127.0.0.1, the pool host's network, or connection-table/idle-timeout behavior under a long-lived busy ssh stream). Note: the unprivileged `toor` user cannot read the system journal, so sshd/kernel logs from the incident windows need the admin's eyes — that is the ask.","created":"2026-08-29T14:22:59-04:00","custom":{"host":"kolu-ci-9"}}
{"id":"sdwz057d","parent":"kolu-ci-downtimes","ord":"a3","title":"2026-08-30 ~14:46 UTC — the whole pool unreachable: the kolu-ci ssh config stanzas are gone from the orchestrator's machine","desc":"**When:** first hit ~14:46 UTC (10:46 ET), 2026-08-30, on #443's CI launch.\n**Symptom:** odu: `ssh: Could not resolve hostname kolu-ci — no reachable host in x86_64-linux pool`. Not one container — the NAME layer: `getent hosts` fails for kolu-ci, kolu-ci-5, kolu-ci-9, and `ssh -G kolu-ci` shows NO config stanza (hostname passes through bare, user srid instead of toor) — the 127.0.0.1 proxy-device Host entries this venue rides are absent from ~/.ssh/config.\n**Context:** the human deployed/rebuilt this morning and their nixos-config session is active — the stanzas are nix-managed, so the likely cause is the in-progress machine-config work, not the containers (yesterday's probe showed the container host healthy, up since Aug 22).\n**Meanwhile:** CI routed to ci@petit (darwin) per the standing either-platform ruling.","created":"2026-08-30T10:48:53-04:00","custom":{"host":"the pool (name layer)"}}
